  "comment": "A root name server is a name server for the Domain Name System's root zone. It directly answers requests for records in the root zone and answers other requests by returning a list of the authoritative name servers for the appropriate top-level domain (TLD). The public root name servers are a critical part of the Internet infrastructure because they are the first step in translating (resolving)",
